#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Aggregate Claude Code token usage across machines.

Claude Code writes one JSONL transcript per session under ~/.claude/projects.
Every assistant record in there carries the model and the API usage counters
of the response it belongs to. This tool reads those files on this machine and
on every SSH host in its config, counts each API response once, and prints
tokens by type, an estimated cost at Anthropic API list prices, and the share
per model and per machine.

Claude Code deletes transcripts after 30 days (cleanupPeriodDays). Every run
therefore merges what it found into a warehouse file, so usage stays counted
after the transcripts are gone. Reports read the warehouse plus fresh scans.

Remote hosts need nothing installed except python3: the tool sends this file
over SSH and runs it there as `python3 - --collect`.

Config (optional): ~/.config/claude-usage/config.json
  {
    "hosts": [
      "tobi.coder",
      {"ssh": "other-box", "name": "other", "projects_dir": "~/.claude/projects", "python": "python3"}
    ],
    "ssh_options": ["-o", "BatchMode=yes", "-o", "ConnectTimeout=20"],
    "timeout": 120,
    "warehouse": "~/.local/share/claude-usage/rows.jsonl",
    "pricing": {"claude-some-model": [5.0, 25.0, 0.5]}
  }

Cost estimates use a built-in price table. Run `claude-usage update` to fetch
current prices from Anthropic's pricing page into
~/.local/share/claude-usage/pricing.json; a report then prefers that file
over the built-in table, and a "pricing" entry in the config above still
overrides both.
"""
